1. What is the Facade Design Pattern?

Problem: A system has multiple complex subsystems/classes, and using them correctly requires calling several of them in the right order. Client shouldn't need to know all that internal wiring.

Solution: Put one simple interface (facade) in front of the complex subsystems. Facade internally coordinates all the subsystem calls. Client just calls one simple method.


Home theater: to watch a movie you'd normally do:

lights.dim();
projector.turnOn();
speakers.setVolume(50);
dvdPlayer.play();

4 objects, 4 calls, specific order. With a facade:

class HomeTheaterFacade {
    void watchMovie() {
        lights.dim();
        projector.turnOn();
        speakers.setVolume(50);
        dvdPlayer.play();
    }
}

// client:
homeTheater.watchMovie(); // one call, hides all the coordination

Core use case: simplify a multi-step / multi-subsystem process into one call.
